The implementation compiles cleanly. Logic: the ringer and motor are only active when `ring` is asserted, and `vibrate_mode` selects which one is on — ensuring exactly one (or neither when `ring=0`) is active, never both.

```verilog
module TopModule (
    input ring,
    input vibrate_mode,
    output ringer,
    output motor
);

    assign ringer = ring & ~vibrate_mode;
    assign motor  = ring & vibrate_mode;

endmodule
```
